[
{
  type: install
  message: <<EOM
The Epithet services are disabled by default. Configure
/usr/local/etc/epithet/server.yaml, install the referenced policy and inventory
files, and generate the CA key before enabling a service.

The service account must be able to read the private key. One suitable setup is:

  chown root:epithet /usr/local/etc/epithet/ca.key
  chmod 0640 /usr/local/etc/epithet/ca.key

Use epithet_server for combined operation, or enable epithet_inventory,
epithet_policy, and epithet_ca for split operation. Do not enable the combined and split modes at
the same time.
EOM
}
{
  type: upgrade
  maximum_version: "0.23.1_1"
  message: <<EOM
This upgrade adds the disabled-by-default epithet_inventory rc.d service.
Move policy.inventory to inventory.static, move policy.principal-mode to
inventory.principal-mode, and move policy.oidc to inventory.oidc. Split CA deployments also
need ca.inventory. Enable inventory alongside policy and CA for split operation.
See docs/inventory.md for the complete migration.
EOM
}
{
  type: upgrade
  minimum_version: "0.23.1_1"
  maximum_version: "0.23.1_3"
  message: <<EOM
This upgrade fixes service startup by ensuring daemon(8), rather than rc.subr,
drops privileges to the epithet account.
EOM
}
]
